{
  "$comment": "PATV text styles (decision 51, §5.5, ADR 0004 rule 9; ADR 0007 D13): the free 16-colour palette, the reserved accents a style may not imitate, and the six fonts. A look's text.color is either one of these palette pairs or any colour a text_style item unlocks, and every colour must pass the same validation (contrast_min against every background of its theme, CIEDE2000 >= delta_e.min from every reserved accent of that theme). v1 owns users.text_style (picker on the Edit profile page) until P-4; the hub validates on apply (H9) and chat-core/looks re-checks before rendering. status stable: the owner confirmed the palette values and reserved accents (ADR 0007 OQ-10, answered 2026-10-19), so they freeze with S1; a later change bumps version.",
  "version": 1,
  "status": "stable",
  "contrast_min": 4.5,
  "delta_e": {
    "formula": "ciede2000",
    "min": 10
  },
